<div class="summary-box">
  <div class="summary-title">🌿 Translator's Summary — Birchas HaPairos &amp; Birchas HaRayach (88–107)</div>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Sections 88–92 (Core Theme):</strong> Why <em>zimun</em> is recited only over bread, not fruits. Bread corresponds to the Torah study that <em>leads to deeds</em> and sustains the world eternally; fruits correspond to studies that only vivify temporarily. The holy gathering (<em>kibbutz</em>) of Israel — built through the <em>tzadik</em>'s <em>remozim</em> (allusions/hints) — is the source of all <em>ratzon</em> (Divine will) manifested at mealtimes.</li>
    <li><strong>Sections 93–97 (Rosh Hashanah, Honey &amp; Bread):</strong> The custom of dipping bread in honey on Rosh Hashanah alludes to rectifying Adam's sin and to our aspiration to taste all the world's flavors within bread itself — as in the manna. The manna-like state is the shofar/Giving of the Torah. <em>Leaven and honey</em> as first-fruits offerings on Shavuos and Rosh Hashanah are explained; the primacy of bread-with-salt as the basic, all-inclusive food is established.</li>
    <li><strong>Sections 98–104 (Land of Israel, Sukkos, Shemini Atzeres):</strong> The seven Species, priority of Eretz Yisroel's fruits in blessings, and the spiritual geography of the Land all correlate to the gathering of Israel around the <em>tzadik</em>-Moshe. Sukkos = <em>Chag HaAsif</em> = gathering of souls and all food-flavors. Shemini Atzeres completes this gathering. Going to <em>tzadikim</em>'s graves in Elul is also connected.</li>
    <li><strong>Sections 105–107 (Birchas HaRayach):</strong> Fragrance (<em>rayach</em>) corresponds to <em>yirah</em> (awe/fear of G-d) and the extraordinary <em>ratzon</em>. The blessing before smelling is sufficient — no final blessing needed — because the entire enjoyment of fragrance is <em>yirah</em> itself, which is already fully present from the moment one makes the blessing. The Land of Israel/Temple = <em>Har HaMoriya</em> = the fragrance of the <em>ketores</em>. Avraham's service was pure <em>ratzon</em> — the added <em>heh</em> in his name signifies this. Good <em>ratzon</em> and holy yearning (<em>kisufin</em>) are the foundation of all spiritual service.</li>
  </ul>
